    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0315" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00113 EW/8–2844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-28T17:00:00+02:00">August 28, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 28—11:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6975. Department’s 6711, August 22, midnight. In accordance with your telegram I
                    have raised informally with Gousev the question of having reparation discussed
                    in Moscow. I explained that this was a personal suggestion of my own which I had
                    made to my Government and was now making to him and that it was not to be
                    regarded as a commitment or expression of definite view on the part of our
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
